{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 9, "model_name": "nvidia/llama-3.3-nemotron-super-49b-v1", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was a member of the House of Arsuf and ruled as Count of Tripoli from 1141 to 1183 he was also regent of the Kingdom of Jerusalem from 1174 to 1183\n\nHe was the son of Hugh II Count of Tripoli and Alice of Jerusalem his mother was a daughter of King Baldwin II of Jerusalem and a sister of King Fulk of Jerusalem and Queen Melisende of Jerusalem\n\n*He played an important role in the politics of the Kingdom of Jerusalem and was a key advisor to King Amalric I who died in 1174 leaving behind a minor son Baldwin IV*\n\nRaymond III succeeded to the county of Tripoli after the death of his father in 1141 he spent several years as a captive of Nur ad-Din after being captured at the Battle of Inab in 1149\n\nHe was released from captivity in 1153 and returned to Tripoli he then played a crucial role in the Siege of Ascalon in 1153 which was a major victory for the Kingdom of Jerusalem\n\n*The County of Tripoli under Raymond III's rule maintained a delicate balance of power with the neighboring Muslim states and the Byzantine Empire through strategic alliances and marriages*\n\nRaymond III married Agnes of Courtenay but the marriage was annulled due to consanguinity he then married Margaret of Hungary but she died in 1168\n\n*Raymond III's regency of the Kingdom of Jerusalem was marked by conflicts with the nobles and the need to manage the leprosy-afflicted King Baldwin IV while fending off threats from Saladin*\n\nRaymond III died in 1183 without an heir and was succeeded by his nephew Hugh IV Count of Cyprus the county of Tripoli eventually passed to the House of Dampierre through the marriage of Hugh IV's sister to Bohemond V Count of Tripoli \n\nThe legacy of Raymond III is complex reflecting both his military failures and his efforts to maintain stability in the region through diplomacy and strategic alliances his role as regent remains a subject of historical debate among scholars. \n\nNote: The word count is 306 words as per your request.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Ray", "logprob": -1.0162889957427979}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": -1.7523612768854946e-05}, {"token": " III", "logprob": -7.879423355916515e-05}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.02725236862897873}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -5.590759246842936e-05}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -1.2397689715726301e-05}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": -2.4199192921514623e-05}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -0.037470437586307526}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.34571248292922974}, {"token": " member", "logprob": -0.6385263800621033}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -1.823885577323381e-05}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.00047267231275327504}, {"token": " House", "logprob": -0.10487507283687592}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -1.0728830375228426e-06}, {"token": " Ars", "logprob": -7.890413284301758}, {"token": "uf", "logprob": -0.023758715018630028}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -0.0478072389960289}, {"token": " ruled", "logprob": -0.24744512140750885}, {"token": " as", "logprob": -0.3571098744869232}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.3953182101249695}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -0.0006350646144710481}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -3.564294092939235e-05}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": -1.9907753085135482e-05}, {"token": " from", "logprob": -0.000527123745996505}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -0.04549144208431244}, {"token": "114", "logprob": -0.06137818843126297}, {"token": "1", "logprob": -2.423351764678955}, {"token": " to", "logprob": -1.1678333282470703}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -0.00860033929347992}, {"token": "118", "logprob": -0.8890730738639832}, {"token": "3", "logprob": -0.2733234763145447}, {"token": " he", "logprob": -1.7239015102386475}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -0.3141140341758728}, {"token": " also", "logprob": -0.616040825843811}, {"token": " reg", "logprob": -1.6067246198654175}, {"token": "ent", "logprob": -1.788